Package: t2-initramfs
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: zhongfu <me@zhongfu.li>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: ZSpace T2 boot initramfs
 The bring-up initramfs the ZSpace T2 (Rockchip RK3568) boots: it resolves and
 mounts the root filesystem named on the kernel cmdline, and with t2.mode=flash
 it runs the installer that writes the eMMC.
 .
 The kernel Image does not embed it.  The boot FIT carries this file as its
 ramdisk subimage, so an on-board kernel upgrade (linux-image-<rel>-t2's
 postinst, which Depends on this package) assembles a bootable FIT from the
 kernel, the board DTB and these bytes.
